{"step_index":72,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T08:34:39Z","content":"Below is a **hands‑on checklist** that you can follow right now – you already have the virtual‑env and the open‑source libraries installed, so the only thing left is to create the **BE‑1 modules** and get them talking to each other.\n\n> **All paths below are absolute** (Windows) and assume the workspace root is  \n\n```\nC:\\Users\\adars_6dx4mbx\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\n```\n\n---\n\n## 📂 1 Create the folder layout\n\n```bat\ncd C:\\Users\\adars_6dx4mbx\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\nmkdir app\nmkdir app\\screen_perception\nmkdir app\\vision\nmkdir app\\calibration\nmkdir app\\mapper\nmkdir app\\bus\nmkdir app\\os_actuator\nmkdir app\\grpc_server\nmkdir tests\nmkdir common\nmkdir common\\proto\n```\n\nAdd an empty `__init__.py` in every new folder so Python treats them as packages:\n\n```bat\nfor /d %d in (app app\\screen_perception app\\vision app\\calibration app\\mapper app\\bus app\\os_actuator app\\grpc_server tests common common\\proto) do echo > %d\\__init__.py\n```\n\n---\n\n## 📜 2 Define the **protobuf contracts** (shared by everybody)\n\nCreate the three `.proto` files in `common\\proto`.  \n\n### 2.1 `actuator.proto`\n\n```proto\nsyntax = \"proto3\";\n\npackage actuator;\n\nservice Actuator {\n  rpc Execute (ActuateRequest) returns (ActuateResponse);\n}\n\nmessage ActuateRequest {\n  enum Type { CLICK = 0; DRAG = 1; TYPE = 2; }\n  Type type = 1;\n  int32 x = 2;\n  int32 y = 3;\n  string text = 4;   // for TYPE only\n}\n\nmessage ActuateResponse {\n  bool ok = 1;\n  string message = 2;\n}\n```\n\n### 2.2 `event.proto`\n\n```proto\nsyntax = \"proto3\";\n\npackage event;\n\nmessage UIElement {\n  int64 id = 1;\n  string name = 2;\n  string role = 3;\n  int32 x = 4;\n  int32 y = 5;\n  int32 w = 6;\n  int32 h = 7;\n}\n\nmessage ScreenEvent {\n  uint64 ts = 1;                // microseconds since epoch\n  bytes png = 2;                // PNG‑encoded screenshot\n  repeated UIElement elements = 3;\n}\n\nenum IntentAction { LOOK_CLICK = 0; LOOK_DRAG = 1; }\n\nmessage Intent {\n  uint64 ts = 1;\n  IntentAction action = 2;\n  int64 element_id = 3;\n}\n\nmessage Result {\n  uint64 ts = 1;\n  bool ok = 2;\n \n<truncated 10942 bytes>\nt (FE‑1, FE‑2, or a manual test) calls the gRPC `Actuator.Execute` RPC.\n\n---\n\n## ✅  Immediate “Next‑Ready‑to‑Run” Checklist\n\n| ✅ | Done? | What to do next |\n|---|-------|----------------|\n| 1 | **Protobuf files** created and Python stubs generated. | Verify `common\\proto\\actuator_pb2.py` etc. exist. |\n| 2 | **Screen capture** (`app\\screen_perception\\capture.py`) runs and publishes `screen.events`. | Open a second console, subscribe with `python - <<PY … PY` to confirm payload size. |\n| 3 | **Vision stub** (`app\\vision\\hand.py`) returns a centre point. | Nothing else needed now. |\n| 4 | **Mapper** (`app\\mapper\\map.py`) can locate an element from the UI list. | Test by running the coordinator (see step 8). |\n| 5 | **ZeroMQ bus** helper (`app\\bus\\bus.py`) available. | Already imported by the scripts. |\n| 6 | **gRPC server** (`app\\grpc_server\\server.py`) starts (stub only). | Run it and keep the console open – later you’ll call it from FE‑1. |\n| 7 | **Coordinator** (`run_pipeline.py`) ties capture → intent together. | Run it; you should see the intent logs. |\n| 8 | **SQLite DB** (optional for now) – you can create it later when BE‑2 starts ingesting events. | No action required now. |\n\nIf every line in the table shows **✅**, you are **ready to start the next BE‑1 phases**:\n\n1. **Replace the vision stub** with a real MediaPipe pipeline (hand landmarks).  \n2. **Add calibration**: show a 3‑point grid, collect hand points, compute the homography, then apply it inside `get_hand_point()` so the hand coordinates map correctly to screen space.  \n3. **Wire the Actuator RPC**: from the intent worker, call the gRPC service (instead of just logging) to perform a real click.  \n4. **Log results** (`hands.result`) into the SQLite DB for BE‑2 to consume.  \n\nLet me know which of those next phases you’d like the **first concrete code snippet for** (e.g., MediaPipe hand detection, homography UI, or a client that calls the Actuator RPC). I’ll provide a ready‑to‑paste implementation. 🚀","thinking":"The user wants help with \"the elements in the list\" as they already have libraries activated. Likely they want to see the step-by-step tasks for BE-1 and maybe code snippets for each. Provide guidance and maybe code skeletons for each element. Provide clear tasks and code examples.\n\nWe should produce concise markdown with tasks, code skeletons, and how to run each. No need to use tools.","truncated_fields":["content"]}
