{"step_index":85,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T08:58:59Z","content":"## What to Do Next – After Adding the Empty `__init__.py` Files  \n\nYou now have a **proper Python package layout** under  \n\n```\nC:\\Users\\adars_6dx4mbx\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\n```\n\nThe next phase is to **populate those packages with the BE‑1 code** that will:\n\n1. Capture the screen and enumerate UI elements.  \n2. Detect (or stub) the hand/gaze point.  \n3. Ask BE‑2’s drift‑detector via HTTP.  \n4. Glide the mouse and click – either on the original bbox (MATCH) or on the healed bbox (DRIFT).  \n\nBelow is a **step‑by‑step checklist** you can follow one item at a time.  \n\n---\n\n### 📦 0 Prerequisite – Verify the virtual‑env\n\n```bat\ncd C:\\Users\\adars_6dx4mbx\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\ncall venv\\Scripts\\activate.bat\npip list   # should show dxcam, mss, pywinauto, pynput, mediapipe, etc.\n```\n\nIf any required package is missing, run:\n\n```bat\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n---\n\n### 📁 1 Generate the protobuf stubs (once)\n\n> The files live in `common\\proto`.  \n> If you already ran this step, you can skip it.\n\n```bat\npython -m pip install grpcio-tools\npython -m grpc_tools.protoc -I .\\common\\proto ^\n    --python_out=.\\common\\proto ^\n    --grpc_python_out=.\\common\\proto ^\n    .\\common\\proto\\actuator.proto ^\n    .\\common\\proto\\event.proto ^\n    .\\common\\proto\\policy.proto\n```\n\nYou should now have:\n\n- `actuator_pb2.py`, `actuator_pb2_grpc.py`  \n- `event_pb2.py`  \n\n---\n\n### 📁 2 Create the **Memory‑client** module  \n\n**File:** `app\\memory_client\\client.py`  \n\nSkeleton (no implementation yet – just the function signature):\n\n```python\n\"\"\"\nMemory client – talks to BE‑2’s drift‑detector over HTTP.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport hashlib\nimport requests\nfrom typing import Tuple, Optional\n\nMEMORY_URL = \"http://172.18.238.74:8000/api/memory/drift-check\"\nTIMEOUT_